# What GitHub's language bar is allowed to count.
#
# `.sergeant/**` carries a lot of shell and Python relative to `src/`, enough
# to skew the bar toward a majority-Shell/Python read of what is a single
# Rust crate. linguist-vendored says "committed, but not ours": the files
# stay tracked and diffable, and stop being counted.
#
# The evidence tree that used to make this worse (`reference/`,
# `reference-corpus/`) moved to `sergeant-rs-workspace` (Phase 4 step 4,
# ADR 0014 decision 17) — a `linguist-vendored` rule here can't reach into
# another repository, so there is nothing to mark for those paths anymore.
.sergeant/** linguist-vendored

# Machine-written, reviewed only as a lockfile.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated
